ng.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u10\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Operational review statement and contact invitation; the practicability qualification concerns SFC enhancements.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the issuing division.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u12\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the issuing regulator.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Closing marker.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope; exhaustiveness is unresolved.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Expands WINGS without adding a separate route requirement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The requirement attaches to applications and submissions concerning investment products administered by IPD. It applies to persons making those submissions, without identifying a particular regulated actor class or creating a general duty to submit.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"e-IP is the investment-product application/submission system on WINGS, whose expansion is supplied. Footnote 1 lists product categories but does not expressly state whether the list exhaustively defines IPD-administered products.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exception is stated. The phrase 'where practicable' qualifies SFC review and enhancement, not the compulsory submission route.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'Must' establishes the compulsory route. Integration and enhancements are announced system changes. 'Can also' describes an optional annual-fee payment facility; the enquiry invitation adds no mandatory filing step.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The 29 July 2024 launch and original 29 October 2024 parallel-run endpoint are historical context. The extension carries parallel running through 29 November 2024, with compulsory e-IP use beginning on 30 November 2024. No express grandfathering rule for pending matters is supplied.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The 8 July 2024 circular and external-authorities.24ec50 dependency are not supplied. Their possible definitions, procedural conditions or exceptions cannot be resolved. Integration of existing IP E-submission requests does not itself establish the underlying reporting triggers or deadlines.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does footnote 1 exhaustively define the covered products, or identify categories within the broader class of products administered by IPD?\\\",\\n    \\\"Does the 8 July 2024 circular or the unavailable external dependency specify exceptions, outage arrangements or treatment of submissions in matters initiated before 30 November 2024?\\\",\\n    \\\"Which existing IP E-submission requests qualify as covered submissions, and what separate sources establish their reporting triggers and deadlines?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run extends its stated feature of accepting existing channels through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The transition applies by the date of each submission event; the supplied text provides no exemption based on when the underlying matter began.\\\",\\n        \\\"Whether a particular product and communication fall within the IPD submission scope must be established separately; unknown classifications remain unknown.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"This reading tests the route used for an individual covered submission from the transition date. It neither makes annual-fee payment through e-IP compulsory nor creates underlying reporting obligations. The strongest uncertainty is the precise product and communication scope, including any qualifications in the unavailable earlier circular. The supplied text does not support a materially different transition date or a general post-transition choice of channels.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The evaluated event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD. Classification must account for footnote 1; optional fee payment alone does not establish this fact.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"is_covered_submission\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"]